These are not incompatible goals. The protection AC means that you can wear
less and get to a survivable AC. Often when doing the MPR I wear banded or
dwarvish mithril. Right now I'm running monks. Such armor is completely
incompatible with the character. When I get the extra AC I can ditch that
armor.

It's easier to get to -10AC starting from naked 1AC than it is to get
there starting from naked 10AC.

Also a non racketeer would have to acqire a lot more money to get to the
same naked AC. A racketeer at XL2 on average would have to spend $5600
to get to naked 1AC (presuming you get an average of 3 points on the initial buy). 
Whereas a player that levels up to XL7 would have to spend $19600 to get
the same protection. Generally the shops and the vaults won't have that
kind of cash. So you'll have to dig deeper into the dungeon to get it. Then
you'll have to travel back to minetown (or to a deeper manned altar in the
main dungeon) in order to purchase that protection.

>Also, it'd be nice if you wouldn't argue with the straw man of people who
>don't believe that weightless AC is a good thing in and of itself.

How can you not? AC is a critical game aspect. Negative AC both reduces your
to hit and takes away some of the damage of hits that get through.

My last game was a perfect example. Got the protection AC. Was crising along.
Decided to take out a priestess at DL10. Screwed up a tried to sacrifice a
white unicorn on a lawful altar (OOPS!). Lost protection. Shortly thereafter
got my ass kicked by a gang of monsters. It's not a direct correlation. But
it does point to the fact that AC is a very important component in the game.

No strategy is risk free. I come around and argue simply because detractors
keep saying that it's extremely high risk when it isn't if run properly.
Early on when I started playing Nethack in the 3.1 era, I ran wizards. My
wizards who got early dragon scale did well, whereas the ones who were not
as well equipped died a lot earlier. I then found out about the protection 
run along with its semi-pacifist strategies. My early game survival rate
went way up. Most of my deaths now occur between the Quest and the castle.

